From: nwrt Xiaomi 14 Pro integration
Subject: [PATCH] qmi: prefer a populated active UIM slot

The Xiaomi dual-SIM firmware reports both physical slots as active even when
the second slot is empty.  The generic loop kept overwriting the primary slot
with the last active entry and therefore selected the empty slot, while the
actual USIM is on slot 1.

Keep each SIM object's active flag, but select the first active slot carrying
an ICCID as the primary slot.  This also avoids issuing a destructive slot
switch merely to work around inconsistent firmware status.

--- a/src/mm-shared-qmi.c
+++ b/src/mm-shared-qmi.c
@@ -3392,2 +3392,6 @@
-            ctx->active_logical_id = slot_status->logical_slot;
-            ctx->active_slot_number = i + 1;
+            /* Some DSDS firmware marks an empty slot active.  Prefer the
+             * first populated active slot instead of the final active entry. */
+            if (!ctx->active_slot_number && slot_status->iccid->len) {
+                ctx->active_logical_id = slot_status->logical_slot;
+                ctx->active_slot_number = i + 1;
+            }
